QUESTION- IF YOU ARE USING VIRTUAL BOX FOR LINUX , ADD A NEW PARTITION FOR MADHAV USER ALLOT HIM 10GB OG SPACE AND CREATE THE MOUNT POINT
ANSWER-

1. Add the 10 GB disk in VirtualBox
Shut down whatever OS your using i am using parrot os.

Go to:
VirtualBox
→ Select Parrot OS
→ Settings
→ Storage
→ Controller
→ Add Hard Disk
→ Create
→ VDI
→ Dynamically Allocated
→ 10 GB

Start Parrot OS.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. Check the new disk

Open a terminal:
command-> lsblk

You should see:

NAME   SIZE TYPE MOUNTPOINTS
sda   50.7G disk
├─sda1   ... part /
└─sda2   ... part
sdb     10G disk

Here:

/dev/sda → Existing disk
/dev/sdb → New 10 GB disk

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Open GParted

Install it if necessary:
command-
sudo apt update
sudo apt install gparted

Open:
sudo gparted

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. Select /dev/sdb

In the top-right corner of GParted, you'll see something like:
/dev/sda (50.70 GiB)

Click it and select:
/dev/sdb (10.00 GiB)
⚠️ Make sure you select /dev/sdb, not /dev/sda, because /dev/sda contains your existing Parrot OS installation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. Create the partition

# If /dev/sdb shows:
unallocated

Right-click the unallocated space:
Right Click

→ New
Set:
File system: ext4
New size:    10240 MiB
Label:       madhav

Then click:
Add

You should now see:

/dev/sdb
└── /dev/sdb1
    ext4
    ~10 GB
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. Apply the changes
Click the green checkmark ✓ at the top.

GParted will ask you to confirm.
Click:
Apply
Wait for it to finish.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. Verify from terminal
Run:
command-> lsblk -f

You should see something similar to:
NAME   FSTYPE FSVER LABEL  SIZE MOUNTPOINTS
sda                         50G
├─sda1 ext4                 ...  /
└─sda2 swap                 ...
sdb                         10G
└─sdb1 ext4        madhav   10G
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8. Create the user
If madhav doesn't already exist:
command-> sudo useradd -m madhav

Set password:
commnand-> sudo passwd madhav

Check:
command-> id madhav

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

9. Create the mount point
Because useradd -m normally creates /home/madhav, check first:

command-> ls -ld /home/madhav
If it exists, don't run mkdir again.
If it doesn't exist:

command-> sudo mkdir -p /home/madhav

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

10. Mount the GParted-created partition

Mount /dev/sdb1:
command-> sudo mount /dev/sdb1 /home/madhav

Check:
command-> df -h /home/madhav

You should see:

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on
/dev/sdb1       9.8G  ...  ...   ... /home/madhav

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

11. Give ownership to Madhav
command-> sudo chown madhav:madhav /home/madhav

#Set permissions:
command-> sudo chmod 700 /home/madhav

Check:
command-> ls -ld /home/madhav

Expected:
output-> drwx------ ... madhav madhav ... /home/madhav

